 }
+
+// DecodeBase64 is cl_http_utility=>decode_base64: Buffer.from(encoded,
+// "base64").toString() — the base64 step of DecodeXBase64 (both alphabets,
+// optional padding, non-alphabet bytes ignored, the content cut at '='),
+// then go/nodeutf8 reads the bytes as UTF-8 text the way Node does: one
+// U+FFFD per ill-formed subpart, valid text around it kept. Oracle: Node
